//! Lane tables of the horizon-legacy-join mod: packet id maps between each
//! lane (the protocol on the wire, e.g. 763 = 1.20.1 or 47 = 1.8.x) and the
//! engine's inner session numbering (upstream's V1_20_3, protocol 765), per
//! state.
//!
//! `table_up`'s array is indexed by the lane's own id and holds the inner
//! session's id for the same packet; `table_down` is the reverse. Both are
//! composed over the packets' prismarine names, with the lane's and the
//! pinned era's own protocol documents, by tools/generate_data.py — the
//! handwritten part of this file never lists a lane.
//!
//! Fallback for a lane with tables whose ids the name match never reached
//! (era renames, packets long gone): the engine drops such a packet instead
//! of sending it, and drops an era payload the pinned reader cannot parse.
//! Joins gate on `covers` (the generated lane list): an unlisted protocol
//! stays with upstream's blanket refusal, never a half-plan of this crate.
//!
//! Regeneration happens in CI on every build; the committed state is what a
//! released .hnmod ships.

/// Whether a lane has tables this build ships: the generated set (see the
/// marker block) regenerates per release through tools/generate_data.py.
/// The engine additionally refuses anything upstream's own adapter already
/// resolves, so only protocols it cannot name reach this gate.
pub fn covers(protocol: i32) -> bool {
    GENERATED_LANES.contains(&protocol)
}

#[rustfmt::skip]
static IDENTITY: [Option<u8>; 256] = identity();

const fn identity() -> [Option<u8>; 256] {
    let mut out = [Option::<u8>::None; 256];
    let mut i = 0usize;
    while i < 256 {
        out[i] = Some(i as u8);
        i += 1;
    }
    out
}

// ---- 8< ---- generated tables (edit only by tools/generate_data.py)
/// The id tables this build ships: one lane per advertised release in
/// the band 47..763 that resolved (tools/generate_data.py derives the
/// set from minecraft-data). lane id -> the inner session's 765-era id
/// by prismarine packet name (clientbound), and the reverse
/// (serverbound), per state and lane. Ids the pinned era does not
/// know by name stay None: the engine drops such packets instead of
/// sending them into the lane wire.

